    "aliases": [],
    "description": "Variable variables refer to a feature that allows to use the value of a variable as the name of another variable. It provides a way to dynamically create and access variables based on runtime values.\n\nVariable variables are denoted by the double dollar sign ``$$`` followed by the name of the variable stored in another variable. More dollar signs may be compounded, though it is rare.\n",
    "code": "<?php\n\n$a = 'b';\n$b = 'c';\n\necho $$b;\n\n?>",
